      "evidence": "**Evidence pointing to higher risk**\n- **The Data Download Program (DDP) is being retired.** This is the Fed's main bulk-download tool. A July 16, 2026 notice says the Board will remove its \"Build Your Package\" (custom download) feature the week of November 9, 2026. It will then remove the preformatted data packages \"later this year and in 2027\" and eventually retire the DDP entirely. Details have not yet been published. ([DDP\u2013FRED page](https://www.federalreserve.gov/data/data-download-fred-information.htm); [DDP home](https://www.federalreserve.gov/datadownload))\n- **This matters for discontinued series.** The release footnotes say the older finance-company new-car loan terms \"remain available from the Data Download Program.\" Their long-term home is therefore tied to a tool that is being shut down.\n- **One data element has been removed.** Since July 2025, retail stores and other non-financial businesses (\"Nonfinancial business\") are no longer a lender category. Totals now include that category only through 2019, so the estimates previously published for 2020 onward are gone from the current figures. (April 7, 2025 announcement; [June 2025 release notes](https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/g19/20250606/))\n\n**Evidence pointing to lower risk**\n- The Board says historical data \"will remain available for download as XML files on statistical release pages.\" It has also published a crosswalk mapping its series IDs to the St. Louis Fed's FRED database.\n- All DDP releases are already in FRED. ALFRED, FRED's archive of past data versions, keeps earlier editions of revised series.\n- Dated past releases (/releases/g19/YYYYMMDD/) are still online.\n- On October 1, 2026, Governor Waller said users \"will soon be routed to FRED.\" That is a move to another Fed-run platform, not a deletion.\n\n**Why Moderate:** No data files have been removed. However, one data element was dropped, and the main tool for bulk historical downloads is being dismantled on a timeline that is only partly announced.\n\n---"
