      "evidence": "**Evidence for higher risk:**\n- The public archive (ESMIS) moved from Cornell's Mann Library to the National Agricultural Library in 2025. Many older links still point to `downloads.usda.library.cornell.edu`, so the risk is broken links, not lost files.\n- The October 2025 issue was never produced because of the government shutdown (NASS notices of 10/31/2025 and 11/19/2025). That is a gap in the series, not a removed file.\n- Routine revisions changed some earlier figures. The biggest was 2025 harvested corn acres: the June 2025 *Acreage* report put them at 86.8 million, and the January final estimate (from the Crop Production Annual Summary) raised that to 91.3 million (Agri-Pulse). This is normal procedure, not data being removed.\n\n**Evidence for No Known Issue:**\n- ESMIS lists every monthly release (e.g., `crop0825.pdf` is still online) in PDF, TXT and ZIP/CSV formats, with an API.\n- Quick Stats and the Historical Track Records (1866\u2013present) remain online.\n- No removed files or data elements were found.\n\n**Rating: No Known Issue.** Earlier data remains accessible and unaltered beyond documented revisions. Keep an eye on link breakage from the archive move.\n\n---"
