      "evidence": "**Evidence for No Known Issue:**\n- **7 U.S.C. \u00a7 2204** is the general mandate to collect and publish agricultural statistics.\n- Some commodities have explicit mandates: cotton (\u00a7\u00a7 471\u2013476, which set report timing), apples (\u00a7 590a) and peanuts (\u00a7 951).\n- The OMB filing for the surveys says the Secretary \"uses estimates of crop production to administer farm program legislation and import and export programs.\"\n- The report feeds USDA's monthly supply-and-demand forecasts (WASDE), Farm Service Agency and crop-insurance programs, and USDA's loan pricing.\n- Crop Production is one of USDA's eight Principal Federal Economic Indicators (FY2027 budget justification), so OMB release rules govern how it comes out.\n- No equivalent public substitute exists; private estimates are proprietary and themselves benchmark to NASS.\n- Congress is protecting the program. The Senate FY2026 committee report (S. Rept. 119-37) directs NASS to \"continue all activities and reports at the frequency assumed in fiscal year 2023.\" The FY2027 budget language requires 30 days' notice to the appropriations committees before any program is discontinued.\n\n**Evidence for higher risk:**\n- \u00a7 2204 itself is broad and does not name the Crop Production report.\n\n**Rating: No Known Issue.**\n\n---"
