      "level": "No Known Issue",
      "evidence": "**Evidence for No Known Issue**\n- I found no reports of any Economic Census files being removed or altered since January 2025.\n- The new Commerce order on confidentiality (DAO 216-26, effective June 4, 2026) applies only to new products. The Census Bureau says products already published \"won't be affected\" ([Census Director's blog, Aug. 2026](https://www.census.gov/newsroom/blogs/director/2026/08/understanding-the-new-disclosure-avoidance-policy.html); [Census Project](https://thecensusproject.org/2026/08/13/standard-deviations-how-will-methodology-restrictions-affect-demographic-and-economic-data/)).\n- Data for 2002\u20132022 remains on the Census Data API, data.census.gov and the bulk download server.\n- Older years are kept in Federal Depository Library Program libraries and HathiTrust.\n\n**Evidence for higher risk**\n- Nothing specific to this dataset.\n- One older change: American FactFinder was retired in 2020, before this period. It changed how users reach the data, not what data exists.\n\n**Rating: No Known Issue.** The past record is intact, and the new confidentiality order doesn't apply to it.\n\n---"
