      "evidence": "**Evidence:**\n- **Questions removed under an executive order.** Following Executive Order 14168, Census removed the gender identity questions through a \"non-substantive change\" request, which avoids public comment (NPR, Feb 21, 2025). The Williams Institute confirms Census \"will not include gender identity questions in future versions of HTOPS\" (Williams Institute public comment, March 2025).\n- **Takedown.** Census removed HPS data and documentation to comply with the OPM \"gender ideology\" memo (Williams Institute; NPR).\n- **Other changes in line with Administration priorities:**\n  - CBAMS was cancelled.\n  - Census was told to eliminate functions not required by law.\n  - A political appointee now runs the bureau.\n  - A Census/BLS/BEA reorganization has been proposed.\n  - The related USDA food security report was ended after USDA called it \"redundant, costly, politicized.\"\n\n**Why High:** The questionnaire has already been changed in direct response to a presidential action, and those changes were approved through the non-substantive change route.\n\n---"
