      "evidence": "**Evidence for High Risk**\n- The statute (Sec. 2610, 42 U.S.C. 8629) requires an annual Report to Congress. The newest one is **FY2022**, published in December 2024.\n- The FY2023 and FY2024 reports have not appeared, and both are well past their statutory deadlines. Reports were already late before 2025, and the April 2025 staff layoffs likely make this worse.\n\n**Evidence for Moderate Risk**\n- The Household Report's approval lapsed for about 4.3 months, from March 31 to August 10, 2026. That is under the one-year line for High Risk ([omb.report](https://omb.report/icr/202606-0970-007); [91 FR 35691](https://thefederalregister.org/documents/2026-11834/submission-for-office-of-management-and-budget-review-annual-report-on-households-assisted-by-the-low-income-home-energy)).\n\n**Evidence for No Known Issue**\n- Data Warehouse updates continue on a regular schedule.\n- The Performance Data Form's approval (0970-0449) runs until June 30, 2028.\n\n**Why this rating:** The required annual report has now been skipped for more than one year, which meets the rubric's \"statutory deadline missed\" test."
