      "evidence": "**Evidence for Gone**\n- On April 1, 2025, HHS laid off the **entire** federal LIHEAP staff (23\u201325 people) and reportedly closed the Division of Energy Assistance ([Sanders letter](https://www.sanders.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/Letter-to-HHS-Secretary-Kennedy-re-LIHEAP-FINAL.pdf); [Guardian](https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/15/rfk-jr-energy-assistance-heat)).\n- In September 2026, 116 members of Congress wrote to HHS about the program running \"without dedicated staff\" and asked how many people work on it ([Pappas](https://pappas.house.gov/media/press-releases/pappas-leads-bipartisan-house-effort-pushing-hhs-to-distribute-liheap-funds)).\n\n**Evidence for High Risk rather than Gone**\n- Money is still flowing: FY2026 base funding of $4.045B was enacted in February 2026.\n- Work continues: the reinstated form lists an OCS contact (Molly Buck), and APPRISE, a contractor, still runs webinars and Warehouse updates.\n- The threat remains: the White House proposed $0 for LIHEAP in both FY2026 and FY2027.\n- Delays are ongoing: funds were released late in FY2025 and FY2026.\n\n**Why this rating:** Losing 100% of dedicated staff, with leadership removed, meets the High Risk test and arguably the staff part of \"Gone.\" I stopped short of Gone because funding continues and the data still comes out through contractors.\n\nI tried the [USAJobs tracker](https://usajobs-tracker.abigailhaddad.com), but its figures load by script and my fetch couldn't read them. The site also says it stopped updating on December 31, 2025."
