      "evidence": "**Evidence by risk level:**\n- **High:** None. There is no statutory deadline, no skipped month, and the OMB approval hasn't lapsed.\n- **Moderate:** The October 2025 funding lapse delayed scheduled releases. The October 2025 advance report came out December 23, 2025, and the full report on January 7, 2026 (Reuters; Census rescheduling notices).\n- **No Known Issue:**\n  - The 2026 releases have been on time. The August 2026 full report came out October 2, 2026, and the next release is set for November 3, 2026.\n  - OMB approval 0607-0008 is active until March 31, 2027 (reginfo.gov, ICR 202312-0607-002).\n  - Census has started renewing it on schedule: a 60-day comment notice for an \"extension, without change\" appeared on July 20, 2026 (91 FR 45236, FR Doc. 2026-14513; comments closed September 18, 2026).\n\n**Rating: Moderate.** The rubric counts delayed publication as Moderate, and the shutdown delays happened within the past year. The current schedule and renewal process otherwise look healthy."
