      "level": "Moderate Risk",
      "evidence": "**Evidence by risk level:**\n- **High:** None specific to M3. There is no executive-order-driven change to the data collection and no negative policy note on the site. The renewal is \"without change.\"\n- **Moderate:**\n  - The FY2026 budget proposes reorganizing BLS, BEA and Census within Commerce.\n  - The same budget commits to eliminating Census functions \"not statutorily mandated or core to the Bureau's mission\" by the end of FY2026 (Census Project; CRS). Because M3 isn't required by name in law, that language could reach it, though its central role in GDP makes that unlikely.\n  - Census has cancelled other surveys (NPR, April 2025), and data has come under wider political pressure, including the widely reported firing of the BLS commissioner in August 2025.\n- **No Known Issue:** What M3 collects and publishes hasn't changed since January 2025, apart from the expanded nondurable detail.\n\n**Rating: Moderate.** Proposed restructuring and the \"non-mandated functions\" directive are pending changes that could affect M3, but nothing targets it directly.\n\n---"
