      "evidence": "**Evidence for No Known Issue**\n- The archive of release PDFs going back to October 1953 is still online; the March 2026 and August 2026 releases (`adv2603.pdf`, `marts_current.pdf`) were retrievable during this check.\n- The time series from 1992 to the present is still on census.gov, the Census API (`timeseries/eits/marts`) and FRED. ALFRED keeps earlier versions back to 2001.\n\n**Evidence for Moderate Risk**\n- The April 2025 revision removed nonemployer businesses from the entire history and moved it to the NAICS 2017 industry codes. The published history was redefined rather than deleted.\n- The 2026 revision (released Sept 28, 2026) changed adjusted figures back to January 2015 and unadjusted figures back to January 2018. It also tied them to the 2023 and 2024 Annual Integrated Economic Survey (AIES), the annual survey that sets the yearly totals.\n- Census overwrites revised figures in its current files. Only the PDF archive and ALFRED keep the numbers as first published.\n\n**Assessment: No Known Issue (close to Moderate).** No files or data fields have been removed. The revisions are documented and follow normal statistical practice, and earlier versions are still available. The 2025 redefinition still means older and newer copies are not comparable, so preservationists should keep copies made before and after April 2025."
