      "evidence": "**Evidence for No Known Issue:**\n- The full series history is still in the public flat files (download.bls.gov/pub/time.series/ei/), the series lookup tool and the API. Headline import data go back to 1982.\n- News releases back through prior years are still in the archive (`/news.release/archives/ximpim_*.htm`).\n- Older versions of the methods handbook are kept (e.g., `/opub/hom/ipp/archive/20240801/`).\n- I found no evidence of past values being removed or rewritten.\n\n**Evidence that might suggest Moderate (but doesn't really qualify):**\n- **October 2025:** 864 of 1,625 indexes have no value. These were never published because of the shutdown; nothing published was taken down.\n- **Discontinued series:** BLS dropped 67 indexes in 2026. Their last published value is December 2025. Past values for dropped series normally stay in the database, but I didn't check each one.\n- **Normal revisions:** Recent values marked \"(R)\" get revised. This is standard practice, not alteration.\n\n**Rating: No Known Issue.** Past data are still accessible and unaltered. The gaps above are missing new data, not removed old data.\n\n---"
