      "evidence": "**Evidence for High Risk:**\n- **The October 2025 release was cancelled outright.** BLS couldn't collect the survey data during the shutdown and can't collect it after the fact. No all-imports or all-exports index exists for that month.\n  - Source: https://www.bls.gov/mxp/notices/2026/2025-federal-government-shutdown-impact-mxpi.htm\n- **Six releases in a row came out late:**\n  - September 2025: moved from Oct 17 to Dec 3, 2025.\n  - November 2025: moved from Dec 16, 2025 to Jan 15, 2026.\n  - December 2025: moved from Jan 15 to Feb 10, 2026.\n  - January 2026: moved from Feb 18 to Mar 5, 2026.\n  - February 2026: moved from Mar 17 to Mar 25, 2026.\n  - The early-2026 delays were caused by a second funding lapse in 2026.\n  - Source: https://www.bls.gov/bls/2025-lapse-revised-release-dates.htm\n\n**Evidence for No Known Issue:**\n- The approval to collect data (OMB No. 1220-0025) is active through 07/31/2027. A minor change was approved 05/21/2026.\n  - Source: https://www.reginfo.gov/public/do/PRAViewICR?ref_nbr=202605-1220-001\n- Since the March 2026 release, data have come out on schedule. The 2026 calendar runs through the November 2026 data, due Dec 17, 2026.\n  - Source: https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/ximpim.htm\n\n**Rating: High Risk.** The rubric puts any skipped collection or publication in the High category, and October 2025 was skipped. This is a borderline call: the skip came from a shutdown, not a decision to cut the program, and releases are back on schedule. If you only count deliberate skips, Moderate would be reasonable.\n\n---"
